WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:08.080
In membranes from cultured cells, the drug paroxetine fills half of the human

2
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.040
serotonin transporters at only 0.08 nM.

3
00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:15.120
Does that explain why some depressed people improve?

4
00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:19.020
It does not. To see why, look at what the drug acts on.

5
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.260
A transmitter works as a system.

6
00:00:22.233 --> 00:00:24.513
A transmitter system has three parts.

7
00:00:25.073 --> 00:00:27.893
The source is the set of neurons that release the chemical.

8
00:00:28.573 --> 00:00:29.813
The readers are the receptors.

9
00:00:30.533 --> 00:00:33.753
Some readers are ion channels, which open within milliseconds.

10
00:00:34.653 --> 00:00:39.533
Others are G-protein-coupled receptors, which act in tens of milliseconds to minutes

11
00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:41.253
through messengers inside the cell.

12
00:00:41.893 --> 00:00:43.573
The off switch ends the signal.

13
00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:46.707
The off switch depends on the transmitter.

14
00:00:47.527 --> 00:00:52.327
Acetylcholine is broken down by an enzyme, acetylcholinesterase, at many synapses.

15
00:00:53.227 --> 00:00:56.047
Glutamate is cleared by transporters in glia and terminals.

16
00:00:56.747 --> 00:00:58.607
No enzyme in the cleft destroys it.

17
00:00:59.147 --> 00:01:00.667
Peptides are cut by peptidases.

18
00:01:01.407 --> 00:01:05.447
The amines, serotonin among them, are carried back into the terminal by

19
00:01:05.447 --> 00:01:09.727
transporters. The serotonin transporter is called SERT.

20
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.760
A drug changes one step.

21
00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:14.740
An agonist activates a reader.

22
00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:19.400
A competitive antagonist takes the reader's own site and prevents activation.

23
00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.440
A positive allosteric modulator binds a different site and strengthens the effect.

24
00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.340
An enzyme inhibitor slows the breakdown.

25
00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:30.220
A reuptake blocker occupies the transporter.

26
00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:35.440
Paroxetine sits in the central site of SERT, where serotonin binds.

27
00:01:36.533 --> 00:01:38.753
How much of the transporter does the drug fill?

28
00:01:39.193 --> 00:01:43.873
The fraction filled is L over KD plus L, where L is the free drug concentration.

29
00:01:44.573 --> 00:01:49.173
The dissociation constant, KD, is the concentration that fills half the sites.

30
00:01:49.873 --> 00:01:56.053
For paroxetine at human SERT in cell membranes, KD is 0.08 nM.

31
00:01:56.613 --> 00:02:00.033
At 0.72 nM, 90% % are filled.

32
00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:01.993
The curve flattens at the top.

33
00:02:02.933 --> 00:02:05.693
Filling the transporter is not a clinical effect.

34
00:02:05.693 --> 00:02:08.753
That these drugs block SERT is established.

35
00:02:09.413 --> 00:02:12.513
That depression is caused by low serotonin is a separate claim.

36
00:02:13.113 --> 00:02:17.653
A disputed 2022 umbrella review found no consistent support for it.

37
00:02:18.093 --> 00:02:23.793
A 2018 network meta-analysis found all 21 antidepressants it included more effective

38
00:02:23.793 --> 00:02:28.533
than placebo for acute major depression in adults, with certainty from moderate to

39
00:02:28.533 --> 00:02:30.753
very low. Both can be true.

40
00:02:31.493 --> 00:02:35.853
Aspirin relieves a headache, and headaches are not caused by a lack of aspirin.

41
00:02:36.533 --> 00:02:39.493
A drug's mechanism does not prove what causes the disease.
